<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 16 December, from 714 to 1991.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-of-herstal" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pepin-of-herstal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">714 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,312 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pepin of Herstal, ruler of the Franks, dies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pepin of Herstal, the mayor of the palace who held real power over the Frankish kingdoms, died at Jupille. After a struggle, his son Charles Martel took control and laid the ground for the Carolingian dynasty.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-of-herstal">Pepin of Herstal</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1431 CE <span class="tih-ago">595 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VI is crowned king of France in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The ten-year-old Henry VI of England was crowned king of France at Notre-Dame. By 1453 the English had lost all their French lands except Calais.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1773 CE <span class="tih-ago">253 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Boston Tea Party</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Colonists, some disguised as Mohawk Indians, boarded three ships in Boston Harbor and threw 342 chests of East India Company tea into the water. Britain's punitive response pushed the colonies towards revolution.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1838 CE <span class="tih-ago">188 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Voortrekkers defeat a Zulu army at Blood River</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A laager of about 470 Voortrekkers repelled thousands of Zulu warriors sent by King Dingane at the Ncome River. The victory became a central symbol of Afrikaner nationalism.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1944 CE <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany launches the Battle of the Bulge</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">German forces attacked through the Ardennes in Belgium and Luxembourg, catching the Americans by surprise. The offensive was contained within weeks and used up Germany's last reserves in the west.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1991 CE <span class="tih-ago">35 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kazakhstan declares independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Kazakhstan became the last Soviet republic to declare independence, days before the USSR was dissolved. Nursultan Nazarbayev led the vast Central Asian country for nearly three decades.</p></div></li></ol>
